We are Team Code Crafters—A, our team lead, along with B, C, and D.
Our challenge was to solve a critical business problem: how can we accelerate the Group Model Validation process for both AI and non-AI models while maintaining quality, governance, and regulatory controls?
To address this, we built a Unified Agentic AI Platform—a Python-based framework powered by six specialized agents orchestrated through an LLM-driven workflow.
Our solution automates key GMV activities such as document review, model assessment, validation, decisioning, and report generation, significantly reducing manual effort and turnaround time. Built using Python, LLM orchestration, JSON-driven configurations, and HTML reporting, the framework supports rule-based, machine learning, and LLM models through a single validation platform.
What makes our solution powerful is its configuration-driven and risk-based approach. Validation policies can be updated without code changes, high-severity findings can automatically trigger failure decisions, and outputs remain consistent, explainable, and fully auditable.
The result is a platform that can reduce validation timelines from months to days or weeks, accelerate model approvals, improve validator productivity, and help the business realize value faster.
Today, we're excited to demonstrate how Agentic AI can transform model validation into a faster, smarter, and more scalable process.

“Our platform starts in main.py, which loads the demo submissions and runs them end-to-end through the validation pipeline. The core logic lives in pipeline.py, where each submission is extracted, classified, matched against policy rules, and then scored using deterministic validators for statistical, fairness, and LLM-related checks. What makes this powerful is that the rules are configuration-driven — the governance logic comes from policy_rules.json and materiality from materiality_matrix.json, so policy updates don’t require code changes. After validation, the framework applies a risk-based verdict, where any high-materiality failure can block approval. Finally, report_generator.py produces both Markdown and HTML reports, so reviewers get a clear, auditable summary with blocking findings, remediation items, and passed checks. In short, this turns model validation from a manual review process into a fast, repeatable, and governed workflow.”


“This output shows our platform in action across four very different model types — from rule-based systems to regression, ML classification, and an underwriting chatbot. It doesn’t just run checks; it turns the results into governed decisions, where low-risk cases pass, missing documentation triggers remediation, and high-materiality issues automatically block approval. You can also see the system catching real fairness and LLM quality problems, including discrepancies between claimed and computed metrics. That’s the value of our approach: faster validation, stronger controls, and clear, auditable decisions.”
